    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-24T17:42:11+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-24T17:42:11+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-24T08:12:11Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-24T08:12:11Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure trough extends from WA over western SA. This trough will be very slow-moving for the rest of this week and over the weekend. A weakening cold front will slip across southern coasts late Thursday and early Friday. Another low pressure trough will develop over WA on Sunday and Monday then move over SA early to mid next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-24T15:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-25T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-24T05:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-24T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Ceduna. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light in the late evening.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-25T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-26T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-24T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-25T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds south to southeasterly and light tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning then tending south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the late afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 12 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 31.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">##</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-26T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-27T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-25T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-26T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. High chance of showers west of Nullarbor, medium chance elsewhere. Winds southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to around 12 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 26.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-27T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-28T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-26T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-27T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Nullarbor, most likely in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h increasing to 30 km/h before turning easterly 20 to 25 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching 22 to 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-09-28T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-29T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-27T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-28T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers west of Nullarbor, most likely in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Nullarbor in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending north to northeasterly during the morning then tending east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
